# REFERENCE ONLY — do not install this file directly.
#
# Use  bash local/bootstrap.sh  instead. It generates these lines with the real
# checkout path for the machine it runs on, and merges them into the existing
# crontab inside a marked block so unrelated cron jobs are preserved.
#
# Installing this file with `crontab local/crontab.et` would REPLACE the whole
# crontab, deleting anything else scheduled on the machine, and the paths below
# are placeholders that will not exist on your box.
#
# Times are Eastern. Set the machine timezone to America/New_York so the
# schedule tracks market hours across DST:
#
#     sudo timedatectl set-timezone America/New_York
#
# Schedule, for reference:
#
#   0  7 * * 1-5   7:00 AM   overnight watch / pre-open brief
#   30 9 * * 1-5   9:30 AM   open reaction, stops + take-profits at the open print
#   0 10 * * 1-5  10:00 AM   first trading session
#   0 12 * * 1-5  12:00 PM   midday trading; last stop check before 3:15
#   15 15 * * 1-5  3:15 PM   close-out, overnight holds, handoff for tomorrow
#   0 10 * * 6    Sat 10 AM  weekly performance review
#
# Each line takes the form:
#
#   <schedule> cd $REPO && claude -p "$(cat local/prompts/<routine>.txt)" \
#       >> $REPO/local/logs/<routine>.log 2>&1
#
# To inspect exactly what will be installed, without changing anything:
#
#     bash local/bootstrap.sh --dry-run
